1
00:00:00,639 --> 00:00:03,479
- What's her name?
- I don't know.

2
00:00:03,642 --> 00:00:05,642
(Sheldon:)And you're going to let her
handle my food?

3
00:00:05,811 --> 00:00:08,151
(Penny:)Nancy. Her name is Nancy.

4
00:00:08,898 --> 00:00:10,778
(Sheldon:)I think you're just making that up.

5
00:00:10,941 --> 00:00:14,741
(Penny:)Sheldon, I'm sorry about your hamburger,
okay? I just don't wanna be a waitress.

6
00:00:14,904 --> 00:00:17,234
(Leonard:)Cheeseburger. I get a cheeseburger.

7
00:00:17,406 --> 00:00:21,076
- Fine. Cheeseburger.
- Maybe I'd be better off with Nancy.

8
00:00:21,702 --> 00:00:24,912
(Penny:)So, what do you think?
I mean, this could be a business, right?

9
00:00:26,290 --> 00:00:29,500
- How many of these can you make a day?
- Mm. About 20.

10
00:00:29,668 --> 00:00:33,258
(Sheldon:)And how much profit do you make
per Penny Blossom?

11
00:00:33,422 --> 00:00:37,472
- I don't know. Like, 50 cents. I'm not sure.
- No, of course you're not. All right.

12
00:00:39,136 --> 00:00:44,266
(Sheldon:)Ten dollars a day times five days a week
times 52 weeks a year is $2600.

13
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:47,440
- That's all?
- Before taxes.

14
00:00:47,603 --> 00:00:50,143
(Penny:)Well, I don't have to pay taxes
on this stuff.

15
00:00:50,314 --> 00:00:53,064
(Sheldon:)The Internal Revenue Service
would strongly disagree.

16
00:00:54,526 --> 00:00:57,656
(Sheldon:)But if you took advantage
of modern marketing techniques...

17
00:00:57,821 --> 00:01:00,021
...and optimized
your manufacturing process...

